SURAKSHA – Women’s Safety & Emergency Response Dashboard

SURAKSHA is an interactive web-based dashboard designed to demonstrate a women’s safety and emergency response system. It brings different safety features together in one interface, including emergency SOS, location monitoring, family safety, ride safety, responder activity, evidence management, and safety analytics.

 🚀 Features

* 🚨 **Emergency SOS** – Simulated SOS alerts and emergency escalation workflow.
* 📍 **Live Location** – Simulated location tracking with coordinates and movement updates.
* 👨‍👩‍👧 **Family Safety** – Trusted contacts, check-ins, and family alerts.
* 🚗 **Ride Safety** – Driver and vehicle information with simulated route deviation detection.
* 🛡️ **Responder Dashboard** – Simulated incidents, responders, response time, and incident status.
* 📁 **Evidence Vault** – Demonstration of consent-based photo, video, and audio evidence management.
* 📊 **Incidents & Analytics** – Safety scores, check-ins, monitored rides, emergency simulations, and route deviations.
* ⚙️ **Safety Settings** – Privacy permissions, location sharing, offline mode, and safety controls.
* 📱 **Responsive Design** – Designed for different screen sizes.

 🛠️ Technologies Used

* HTML5
* CSS3
* JavaScript
* Responsive Web Design
* Dashboard UI
* Data Visualization

 🎯 Project Objective

The objective of SURAKSHA is to demonstrate how multiple women’s safety features can be organized into a single interactive dashboard. The project focuses on user interface design, interactive components, JavaScript functionality, and presenting safety-related information in an easy-to-understand format.

 ⚠️ Important Note

This project is a **front-end demonstration only**. GPS tracking, SOS alerts, emergency dispatch, responder actions, camera/microphone access, and other emergency functions use **mock or simulated data**. The project does not connect to real emergency services.

